# SELinux rules for the minigbm gralloc4 allocator
# (android.hardware.graphics.allocator@4.0-service.minigbm -> hal_graphics_allocator_default)

# --- CMA dma-buf heap (v3d / Raspberry Pi) ---
# The v3d minigbm backend allocates shared/scanout/CPU-visible buffers from the
# CMA dma-buf heap and imports the dma-buf into v3d via PRIME, instead of
# borrowing a CMA BO from vc4. The heap node is the board's CMA area, e.g.
# /dev/dma_heap/linux,cma on bcm2712, which AOSP's file_contexts labels with the
# catch-all `dmabuf_heap_device` (only /dev/dma_heap/system* get the
# dmabuf_system_heap_device label that is granted by default).
#
# r_file_perms is enough: v3d_open_cma_heap() opens the heap O_RDONLY and
# DMA_HEAP_IOCTL_ALLOC needs no more than that (same as libdmabufheap).
#
# Only the allocator gets this. coredomain (surfaceflinger, system_server, apps)
# has a neverallow on non-system heaps (system/sepolicy/private/coredomain.te),
# so the gralloc *mapper* copy of the backend, which is dlopen()ed into those
# processes, deliberately runs with no heap fd — it never allocates, and it
# maps heap-backed buffers through the PRIME/V3D_MMAP_BO path instead.
allow hal_graphics_allocator_default dmabuf_heap_device:chr_file r_file_perms;
